Necessity, the Mother

Free will is what presumably makes us different from other animals. We believe we have a unique ability to choose and act freely. (See Free Will: Fack or Wishful Thinking?, p.586) The well-known proverb, &#8220;Necessity is the mother of invention&#8221;, points to the actual truth. Simply put, necessity is the mother of all choice and [&hellip;]
